Z||000000||Ironhorse||05-04-2001||12:15 AM||||Hey there.  My friend has a computer, and his wife live 5 hrs away taking care of her ill father has WebTV.  She is not able to use program like AOL instant messenger so that she and her husband can chat back and forth easily and quicker than e mail.  I'm wondering if there's something available that's similar to AOL instant messenger that can be use.   Thanks in advance||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-04-2001||12:18 AM||||Yahoo has a Chat section. It's free to join and works good. They can also set up a "private" room so that they are the only ones in it and can talk without being "eave's dropped" on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||05-04-2001||08:15 AM||||Most of the common messaging systems like Instant Messenger or ICQ won't work on WebTV.  You're pretty much limited to anything accessible with a browser, like Orief's suggestion of yahoo chat, or other places like talkcity, poolsite chat, etc.(Any of you remember firefly.com?)<P>To touch on Orief's comments, "private" is a misnomer BTW, the sysops can still monitor your conversations and everything you say is logged.  Unless you're using a service like anonymizer you aren't anonymous either.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>Yahoo has a Chat section. It's free to join and works good. They can also set up a "private" room so that they are the only ones in it and can talk without being "eave's dropped" on.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Oreif||05-04-2001||09:27 AM||||Sorry, I didn't mean that it was totally a "private" room, Private room just means that no other users can enter the room and detract from or join in the conversation. Other users have to be "invited" in. Yes the sysop's and moderator's can monitor the room's like LaryyB says.||||reg||1
